# Medora enterprise locale isolation (MEDUI.CP.1F.3)

**Short form:**

> **UI chrome follows session locale. Template activation snapshots in intended clinical locale. Persisted clinician narrative is never silently machine-translated.**

## CORE INVARIANT

A Medora UI session must resolve:

| Kind | Rule |
|---|---|
| **A. UI chrome** | Localize dynamically from session locale (`en` \| `fr` only) |
| **B. Reusable template source** | Resolve at activation using authoritative activation locale |
| **C. Patient-specific persisted clinical narrative** | Historical snapshot — do not retranslate on locale switch |
| **D. Clinician-written narrative** | Never machine-translate |

## Cross-language display

- **EN session** must not receive **FR** template-derived narrative on **new** activation.
- **FR session** must not receive **EN** template-derived narrative on **new** activation.
- The only acceptable cross-language display is **persisted historical** clinician or activation snapshot text documented in that language.

## Activation locale authority

Preferred order (validate `en` \| `fr` only):

1. Authenticated user's resolved UI / documentation locale (client sends; API validates)
2. Facility configured language (when applicable)
3. Product fallback (`MEDORA_CARE_PLAN_CLINICAL_LOCALE_FALLBACK`)

**Never** hardcode a single locale for every activation globally.

## Clinician-facing surfaces

Overview, Clinical Context, Summary, Print, Active Care Plan, History, Correction — must consume canonical clinical text projection/resolvers.

**Never** display raw i18n keys, template IDs, or internal enum paths to clinicians.

## Regression hook

Before shipping clinical template or overview work:

1. Audit activation locale source (not hardcoded global default).
2. Assert clinician-facing output contains **zero** matches for internal key patterns (`enterpriseInterdisciplinaryCarePlans`, `.templates.`, `.goalBody`, etc.).
3. Confirm persisted narrative unchanged when UI locale switches.
